  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \n\nA cold front will push through the area Wednesday night into \nThursday, bringing widespread precipitation. Some models are \nshowing a few areas getting over an inch, but most of the \nregion should receive much lower amounts. There is a 10% chance \nthat some areas in Ohio and northeast Kentucky could get 2 \ninches. Models continue to struggle with precipitation amounts\nhowever, so confidence is low. Despite some decent shear and \nlow level helicity values, small CAPE values should prevent \nstrong storms, although a rumble of thunder is possible.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nMuch cooler air will move in behind the front for the weekend. \nA series of upper level disturbances will move over the area for\nthe weekend and into the next work week. This will leave some \npossibility of showers at times.",
